{"seq":16,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/openclaw-opus-gbrain-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T09:47:57.826Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"7dc1bf58c79a48a3d60805cd2db5b954873caad3e6c173170b672fa01f5cbe26","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes I could find (the six public digests under the North and Central team folders). Two ticket numbers mention Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in at Dock Doors 14–18 at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their SMS bay assignments. Support patched it on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the fix worked. The note also has a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. It went to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThe other QFL mentions have no ticket number. These are the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest (Thea's appointment time vs. gate arrival question) and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in. The Central digests have tickets #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those are for other accounts, not QFL. Also, Marcus's \"Quarendon Freightways\" intel note is about a competitor, not our customer, so I left it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
